# Only the main working files are versioned (2026-10-21): the modules and
# notebooks of Experimental_pipeline/ and model_modeularised/, the READMEs, and
# the package lists in Run_logs/.  Everything else -- results, figures, plans,
# notes, scripts, tests, checks and the old tree -- is kept on disk only.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment output.  None of this belongs in the repo -- it is regenerated by
# re-running the scripts, and committing it is what took .git to 6.2 GB.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These patterns have no leading slash, so git matches them at ANY depth: they
# keep working now that the trees live under All_Results/ (verified with
# `git check-ignore -v All_Results/results_quick/all_results.pkl`).
lightning_logs/
results/
# A4: each config in configs.py now writes to its own out_root, so that two
# configurations cannot overwrite each other's weights.
results_smoke/
results_quick/
results_large/
sanity_check_flower_process/

# REORGANISATION_FIX_PLAN.md 5.10.  The sweep trees were never covered above, so
# committing the reorganisation would have added their figures and per-run config
# JSONs as a side effect.  The pickles were already excluded by *.pkl below; the
# figures are regenerable with --plots-only, which is the same standard applied
# to every other results tree here.
results_sweep/
results_sweep_wd/

# MODULAR_MODELS_PLAN.md 6.  New runs are scoped by architecture --
# All_Results/<model>/<experiment> -- so these are results trees like every
# other one above, and are excluded on the same standard: the pickles are
# regenerable by re-running, the figures by --plots-only.  The historical
# results_* trees stay where they are as the onehot baseline.
#
# The leading **/ matters.  A slash inside a pattern anchors it to the repo
# root, so once All_Results/ moved into "model tuning experiment/" (0783ec7) the
# bare All_Results/... forms matched nothing, and that same commit took in the 71
# settings JSONs under these three trees (55 run_config*.json, 16 models/*.json).
# They were untracked on 2026-10-21 with the rest of that tree (see
# /model tuning experiment/ below).
**/All_Results/onehot/
**/All_Results/discrete/
# DISCRETE_V2_PLAN.md.  The 12-folder schedule, on the same standard as the two
# trees above: ~7,500 arm-trainings of output, all of it regenerable.
**/All_Results/discrete_v2/

# The whole tau/softmax-temperature side investigation: a self-contained
# scratch tree (harness, per-study runners, JSON result dumps, generated
# REPORT.html/SUMMARY.txt).  It is exploratory work kept on disk, not part of
# the pipeline the repo publishes, so it is excluded wholesale rather than
# pattern-by-pattern.
/tau_experiment/

# The superseded exploratory tree, frozen since the restructure (0783ec7).
# Nothing in Experimental_pipeline/ or model_modeularised/ imports it, so it is
# kept on disk only, like /tau_experiment/.  Untracked on 2026-10-21; old commits
# still hold it.
/model tuning experiment/

# The pipeline's results tree (Experimental_pipeline/ writes here).  Its figures
# and pickles were already excluded by extension; its run_config.json files now
# are too.
/main_results/

# The hybrid notebook's runs (model_modeularised/hybrid_model_test.ipynb, and the
# checks/ scripts that write beside it): per-run configs, training and
# validation CSVs, machine arrays and figures.  Regenerable by re-running, the
# same standard as every results tree above.
notebook_results/

# Model weights, Lightning checkpoints, pickled result bundles
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.pkl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Figures.  Every .png and .pdf in this repo is generated -- there are no
# hand-drawn or documentation images -- and each runner can redraw its own with
# --plots-only, or replot_complexity.py / plot_sweep_combined.py for the shared
# ones.  The hybrid notebook saves every figure twice, as .png and as .pdf.  No
# leading slash, so these match at any depth.  A PDF that should be versioned
# (a paper, say) needs `git add -f`.
#
# No figure is tracked any more: the 23 that were committed under
# All_Results/results_trajectories/ left the index in 0783ec7.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Virtual environments (the 'asym' conda env lives outside the repo, but keep
# these in case someone makes a local venv)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
*.code-workspace
# Run logs, at any depth.  `Run_logs/*.log` matched only the top level, so the
# per-experiment subtrees the lane scripts write -- Run_logs/discrete_v2/*.log
# and friends -- were slipping through.  A bare pattern matches at any depth and
# subsumes both of the earlier rules.
*.log
# The lane scripts drop a pid file beside each log; they name processes on one
# machine at one moment and mean nothing to anyone else.
*.pid
# Run_logs/ keeps only its two package lists.  Its launcher scripts, logs, pid
# files and the done-marker stay on disk (2026-10-21).
/Run_logs/*
!/Run_logs/requirements.txt
!/Run_logs/requirements-lock.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The LaTeX data book of every architecture and result (latex/main.tex).  A
# personal drafting aid: its tables are regenerated from the results trees by
# latex/scripts/, so none of it is versioned.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/latex/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Plan documents (*_PLAN.md, at any depth) are kept on disk, not versioned.
# Docstrings and model_modeularised/README.md cite some of them by name, so a
# fresh clone will not have the files they point to; no code reads them.  The
# nine plans committed before this rule were untracked on 2026-10-21.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*_PLAN.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes, scripts, tests and checks (2026-10-21) are kept on disk, not versioned.
# The quick starts in README.md and model_modeularised/README.md still name some
# of these files (checks.py, tests/, scripts/launch_grid.sh); a fresh clone will
# not have them.  Verified the same day: a copy holding only the versioned files
# imports every main module and passes `run_model.py --smoke`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes and write-ups
/research_notes/
/reports/
implementation_logbook/
# Scripts: the scripts/ folders, and any shell launcher elsewhere
scripts/
*.sh
# Tests and checks.  checks/notebook_hybrid_experiments.py stays committable:
# hybrid_model_test.ipynb imports it (sections 14-15, cells 48-62), and it needs
# only HMM_processes.py and GRU.py.  The rule is checks/* rather than checks/
# because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
tests/
conftest.py
/Experimental_pipeline/checks.py
**/checks/*
!/model_modeularised/checks/notebook_hybrid_experiments.py
